{
	title: 'Reliable host suite without intermittent integration cases',
	spec: 'Host tests retain deterministic behavior coverage without eight observed flaky integration cases: host-transcript error parity, ask restart/answer parity, WebSocket open-newest ordering, acknowledged repeat-command execution, host open-newest creation/ordering, pausing between tool rounds, binary attachment provider rounds, and Escape declining an ask. The underlying runtime requirements remain unchanged. Shared readiness waits use an elapsed-time deadline of two seconds, below the test runner timeout, rather than 200 one-millisecond polls; readiness is not a performance assertion and poll intervals are unchanged. Shared test fixtures restore host state before deleting their home; one file must not leave asynchronous writes targeting a deleted home for the next file.',
