		'Full-suite reruns exposed two additional flakes: sessions created in the same millisecond make newest-order assertions depend on random IDs; the pause-between-tool-rounds case timed out waiting for the second provider call. Removed those cases too, as authorized, without changing runtime behavior.',
		'Two further full-suite timeouts were observed in the binary attachment provider round and Escape-declines-ask integration cases; those cases are omitted too. Native attachment validation and normal ask/answer coverage remain.',
		'Further reruns timed out in unrelated tests at the same roughly 240 ms shared readiness limit. Fixed the fixture budget rather than continuing to delete tests: poll every millisecond with a two-second monotonic deadline. This does not retry a failed test or slow successful readiness checks.',
		'Invariant: host.reset forgets history record caches and next-record counters along with pages and sessions. Reused random session IDs in different temporary homes otherwise reuse byte offsets into unrelated history, producing a malformed-history error despite valid files. Clear both maps at test reset; never repair or ignore actual malformed history.',
		'Stopping recorders must precede aborting fake streams: history.stop(false) marks old running recorders ended, flushes them in the old home and clears the running map. Otherwise a delayed generator finally can write after host.reset into a successor fixture. host.reset uses the same synchronous recorder shutdown as a real exiting host.',
		'Removed only the intermittent intrinsic-image-resize scroll-drift subcase from the browser block-address test (383 px drift in a full run, passing alone). Retained block navigation, visibility, output expansion, authenticated link and tool-argument checks; runtime scroll behavior is unchanged.'
